WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:13.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Friday the eighth of May. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the silent Teams briefing again?</v>

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:19.050
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, we've got you. Bit tinny, but that might just be the office speakers.</v>

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.660
<v Hannah Price>Morning. Anyone watch the football last night? Honestly, those last few minutes.</v>

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:32.030
<v David Whitfield>Saw the result. Glad I didn't stay up for it, by the sound of you.</v>

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.359
<v Hannah Price>Ninety minutes of my life I'm not getting back.</v>

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:44.899
<v Jamie Brennan>I'm more interested in the weekend weather. Had plans for a barbecue, now it looks like standing under an umbrella with a sausage.</v>

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.929
<v Fiona Doyle>So, a normal British barbecue.</v>

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:55.859
<v David Whitfield>At least there's the charity bake sale on Friday. Today, I mean. Still mentally on Wednesday.</v>

00:00:56.509 --> 00:01:00.009
<v Grace Liu>It's been that sort of week. Cake sounds about right.</v>

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.799
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the catering meeting. Let's do the finished stuff first.</v>

00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:14.760
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah so, tested the site water yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished, nothing outstanding from that.</v>

00:01:15.489 --> 00:01:18.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, closed rather than another job on today's list.</v>

00:01:20.269 --> 00:01:25.870
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I finished the repair on the GT2 inlet valve last night. That's done as well.</v>

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.819
<v David Whitfield>Right, the inlet valve repair's complete. Got you.</v>

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.010
<v Sarah Okafor>I tested the GT2 bearing yesterday and it's all fine now, too. That check's closed.</v>

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.299
<v Tomasz Nowak>One observation, though. Heard a slight rattle from the Line 3 Chiller. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:48.500
<v Fiona Doyle>Just an observation, then, not a maintenance job coming out of this?</v>

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.060
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. Not asking for any work on it.</v>

00:01:55.400 --> 00:02:05.900
<v David Whitfield>Similar sort of thing: saw the pressure on the WHB dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own. Just reporting what I saw, no action from that.</v>

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:16.699
<v Jamie Brennan>And the 11kV board is still waiting on parts. Nothing we can do until they arrive, so that's blocked, not something we can progress today.</v>

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Let's keep the blocked stuff separate from what we're actually agreeing.</v>

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:28.830
<v Fiona Doyle>Please. Otherwise the list looks twice as long and half of it's already finished.</v>

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:36.500
<v Sarah Okafor>On purchasing, could you chase the purchase order for the turbine one compressor, Fiona? No rush.</v>

00:02:37.789 --> 00:02:43.740
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, I can't take that one. I haven't got the purchasing access to follow it through properly.</v>

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:51.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Jamie, can you take that instead—chase the purchase order for the turbine one compressor? Still no rush.</v>

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:57.310
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the turbine one compressor. That's with me instead.</v>

00:02:59.759 --> 00:03:03.610
<v Fiona Doyle>Thanks. Better than me bouncing it straight back to Stores anyway.</v>

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.840
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, no rush, understood. Not treating it as an urgent chase.</v>

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:19.210
<v Grace Liu>While we're on that, we were going to replace the belt on the turbine one compressor, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it. Not work for today.</v>

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, belt replacement out of today's scope. The purchase order chase is separate.</v>

00:03:26.729 --> 00:03:33.729
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll book a contractor to look at the GT2 this morning. No rush on that, just a routine booking.</v>

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:40.330
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's the booking this morning, not saying the contractor's coming this morning?</v>

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. I'll make the booking this morning; we're not agreeing an attendance time here.</v>

00:03:47.719 --> 00:03:50.870
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it, Sarah. Yours, and not an urgent call-out.</v>

00:03:52.169 --> 00:03:57.069
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fine. Just didn't want that muddled with the inlet valve repair I've already finished.</v>

00:03:58.659 --> 00:03:59.860
<v Sarah Okafor>No, definitely separate.</v>

00:04:01.969 --> 00:04:06.520
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, you both came through together for a second. I've got it now.</v>

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:14.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, if you've got a spare minute, could you send the shift handover report round by Thursday?</v>

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:20.470
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round by Thursday.</v>

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. It's an if-you've-got-a-spare-minute one, not something to drop everything for.</v>

00:04:26.949 --> 00:04:28.699
<v Grace Liu>Understood. Low-key, but by Thursday.</v>

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.800
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, was that me making the echo?</v>

00:04:32.569 --> 00:04:35.720
<v Jamie Brennan>Think so. It's gone now. Teams keeping us humble.</v>

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:42.449
<v Grace Liu>Also, I'll inspect the turbine two water valve for leaks this afternoon. That one's fairly important.</v>

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:48.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Grace Liu on the turbine two water valve inspection this afternoon, fairly important.</v>

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.230
<v Grace Liu>Yep, I'll do the leak inspection. That's mine.</v>

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:57.649
<v Tomasz Nowak>Clear. Turbine two water valve, separate from the site water testing that's already done.</v>

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.500
<v Grace Liu>Exactly, different item.</v>

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:05.930
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, easy to merge those in your head when everything's got water or turbine in the name.</v>

00:05:07.149 --> 00:05:13.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Last one. David Whitfield, could you write up the near miss at the palletizer for tomorrow at 9:30?</v>

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:19.339
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll write up the near miss at the palletizer. Tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:26.730
<v David Whitfield>That's Saturday, just saying it out loud so my brain doesn't turn it into Monday.</v>

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, tomorrow at 9:30 is the deadline.</v>

00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:32.209
<v David Whitfield>Understood.</v>

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:39.740
<v Fiona Doyle>That all sounds clear. And the chiller rattle and WHB pressure dip are observations only.</v>

00:05:40.649 --> 00:05:43.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Neither is a new job from this meeting.</v>

00:05:45.839 --> 00:05:50.389
<v Jamie Brennan>And no magic progress on the 11kV board while the parts aren't here.</v>

00:05:50.899 --> 00:05:55.100
<v Tomasz Nowak>Would be nice if saying it on Teams made the parts appear.</v>

00:05:57.439 --> 00:05:59.540
<v Hannah Price>Usually just makes another notification appear.</v>

00:06:00.379 --> 00:06:04.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. Finished work stays closed, blocked work stays separate. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:10.240
<v David Whitfield>Cheers. Glad we've established what day it is, at least.</v>

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.410
<v Grace Liu>Friday. Definitely Friday. See you in a bit.</v>
